  "notes": "Names: the west-edge street is printed QUARRY ... STREET north of about y 2700 and LEEPER ... AVE. from Colerain Avenue up to Kentucky Avenue; I used Leeper Avenue at Kentucky. The avenue with 43xx/42xx house numbers from the Kirby fork (2697,1540) down to Chase is labelled only AVE.; I call it Virginia Avenue because it runs straight into the street printed VIRGINIA south-west of Chase and the house numbers continue. Kirby Avenue (60 ft) continues south-south-east from the fork, off this strip, and comes back as the street printed KI... at x about 2770 on Chase, crossing Hanifield at (2668,5613). N BADGLY (no suffix printed) south of Tarrant lines up with the avenue labelled AVE. north of Tarrant, recorded as one street, North Badgly Avenue; the same line reappears as the Badgly Avenue stub north of Kentucky (printed BADGLY south of Washburn). The street along y 1325 (25 ft, then a 30 ft diagonal to Martha) has only ST. printed in this strip: '?'. Georgia and Florida are printed without a clear suffix south of Chase (a T and an S of ST. are visible) and their legs north of Chase are labelled only AVE.; Florida's northern leg runs to Bruce Avenue and is recorded as Florida Avenue there. Leher Street (30 ft) widens and continues as Chase Avenue (50 ft) at (775,4243). Chase Avenue is offset at Virginia Avenue: the north-west leg meets it at (1323,4743), the east leg at (1445,4650). The road leaving Colerain Avenue to the west at (664,5212) has only RD. on the plate. Lambston is my reading of the label (LAMBSTON), about 20 ft wide. Agate Alley is my reading of the short alley between Hemlock and Cypress Alleys. Block 62 (Jerome to Georgia) has unnamed 12 ft alleys, not picked. Lines marked 12' W. and 18' W. between Leher Street, Lambston and the foot of Carlin look like private ways, not picked. Chase x Kirby (x about 2775) is past the 2700 limit and not picked."
